  "text": "��이터 of weights \\( p, 2p, 3p, 4p, 15 \\) grams. There are only blue and black boxes available. Blue boxes can hold as much weight as all 5 boxes combined, and red box can hold 6 times as much as the blue box. What is the mass of the blue box filled with all 5 weights?\n\nTo solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total weight of all five weights.\n2. Determine the maximum capacity of the blue box.\n3. Determine the capacity of the red box, which is 6 times the capacity of the blue box.\n4. Determine the mass of the blue box filled with all five weights.\n\nLet's start by calculating the total weight of all five weights:\n\n\\[ p + 2p + 3p + 4p + 15 = 10p + 15 \\]\n\nThe maximum capacity of the blue box can hold as much weight as all five weights combined, so the capacity of the blue box is \\( 10p + 15 \\) grams.\n\nThe red box can hold 6 times the capacity of the blue box, so its capacity is \\( 6 \\times (10p + 15) = 60p + 90 \\) grams.\n\nSince the red box can hold 6 times the capacity of the blue box, and the blue box's capacity is \\( 10p + 15 \\) grams, we need to find the value of \\( p \\).\n\nSince the red box's capacity is \\( 60p + 90 \\) grams, and it can hold 6 times the capacity of the blue box, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 60p + 90 = 6 \\times (10p + 15) \\]\n\nLet's solve this equation for \\( p \\):\n\n\\[ 60p + 90 = 60p + 90 \\]\n\nThis equation holds true for any value of \\( p \\), so we need to determine the capacity of the blue box filled with all five weights. The mass of the blue box filled with all five weights is \\( 10p + 15 \\) grams.\n\nLet's use Python to verify this solution.\n```python\n# Define the variables\np = 1  # p can be any positive value, we can use 1 for simplicity\n\n# Calculate the total weight of all five weights\ntotal_weight = 10 * p + 15\n\n# The capacity of the blue box is the total weight of all five weights\nblue_box_capacity = total_weight\n\nprint(blue_box_capacity)\n```\n```output\n25\n```\nThe capacity of the blue box filled with all five weights is \\( 10p + 15 \\) grams. For \\( p = 1 \\), the mass of the blue box filled with all five weights is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) grams.\n\ndef update_frequency_table(freq_table, product):\n    '''\n    This function updates the frequency table with a new product.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    freq_table (dict): A dictionary containing products and their frequencies.\n    product (str): The new product to be added to the dictionary.\n    \n    Returns:\n    None: The function modifies the frequency table in place.\n    '''\n\n数据展示spreadsheet\n sheet_name\nstop list\ndata list\n\nAs\ndef is_product_in_list(product, stop_list):\n    '''\n    This function checks if a product is in a given stop list.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    product (str): The product to be checked.\n    stop_list (list): The stop list to check against.\n    \n    Returns:\n    bool: True if the product is in the stop list, False otherwise.\n    '''\n\n Т",
